body: "## Tested revision and evidence\n\nPR [#274](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/pull/274), head `f2ccb91f3db62fa404e3d10b0af386612ebc5412` (still current when rechecked on 2026-10-28 at approximately 17:03 UTC).\n\nBoth final-head jobs in run 40728719161 finished with **850 passing and 2 failing tests**:\n- [Node 22, job 122958888834](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/actions/runs/40728719161/job/122958888834), completed 16:55:15 UTC.\n- [Node 26, job 122958890207](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/actions/runs/40728719161/job/122958890207), completed 16:50:44 UTC.\n\nThis is hosted CI evidence plus exact-source inspection, not a claim that these full integration suites were rerun locally or that the draft PR is deployed.\n\n## 1. The named compatibility matrix depends on the host installation\n\nThe new [item-history-versions test](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/blob/f2ccb91f3db62fa404e3d10b0af386612ebc5412/test/item-history-versions.test.ts#L21-L28) uses the repository's existing `node_modules/@unbrained/pm-cli` for the 2026.10.20 case and only materializes other named versions into separate prefixes. In both CI jobs, the package at that location is 2026.10.23. The strict assertion fails at line 28:\n\n```text\nactual:   '2026.10.23'\nexpected: '2026.10.20'\n```\n\nThe test correctly refuses to mislabel the artifact, but this means CI does not complete the promised .20/.27/.28 compatibility matrix. Expected: every named version is obtained and verified independently of the consumer's current dependency installation, without changing the project's certified pins.\n\n## 2. The new summary projection breaks an existing history consumer assertion\n\nThe real HTTP lifecycle test [pm-collaboration.test.ts:516–518](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/blob/f2ccb91f3db62fa404e3d10b0af386612ebc5412/test/pm-collaboration.test.ts#L516-L518) retrieves history after a mutation with reason `exercise update flags`, then expects that reason in the response. The new route returns only index/timestamp/action/author rows. Both jobs receive a successful page containing create/update/comment_add/note_add/append, but no reason, and fail the assertion.\n\nPatch-free summaries and bounded default output are useful. The unresolved part is how a consumer explicitly retrieves historical mutation reasons/detail after the API contract change. Do not treat simply deleting the assertion as evidence that the complete lifecycle capability is preserved. This does **not** show that persisted history was erased; it shows that an existing HTTP retrieval contract no longer exposes the expected fact.\n\n## Scope, owner and acceptance\n\nThe canonical [pm-web-lgg5 item](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/blob/f2ccb91f3db62fa404e3d10b0af386612ebc5412/.agents/pm/issues/pm-web-lgg5.toon) explicitly requires real .20/.27/.28 output and full npm/Bun gate evidence. It remains in progress. [pm-web-f3xo](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/blob/f2ccb91f3db62fa404e3d10b0af386612ebc5412/.agents/pm/issues/pm-web-f3xo.toon) separately owns backwards-cursor efficiency; this report does not duplicate that work or upstream ordering issue unbraind/pm-cli#1617.\n\n- Materialize and assert each claimed compatibility version in isolated directories, including 2026.10.20, independently of the host dependency version. Preserve existing project pins.\n- Run all nine documented projection cases on Node 22 and Node 26 rather than stopping at the first version assertion.\n- Keep compact paginated defaults, but explicitly preserve historical reason/detail retrieval through an authorized supported projection or detail path, or document an accepted API migration and its equivalent retrieval mechanism.\n- Update lifecycle tests to exercise both bounded summary behavior and the retained reason/detail capability. Preserve membership checks, typed refusals, append-safe pagination and stale-cursor behavior.\n- Re-run the full npm/Bun gates on the final immutable head and record completed counts. Keep failed, pending and superseded results distinct.\n\nIndependent bounded verification passed 17 extracted-helper checks across this history implementation and the separate Ops #224 review. The Web subset passed 8 checks for ordering, bounds, 125-row pagination across an append, cursor scope/staleness and truthful errors. Those mocked-boundary helper checks do not override the real integration failures above.\n\nDuplicate check: reviewed all 274 all-status repository issues/PRs, current #274 conversation and inline review comments, and both linked PM records. No existing issue records this pair of current CI failures. Closed #249 concerns an unrelated browser-baseline declaration fixture. The existing CodeQL comment is a separate scanner finding and is not duplicated or classified as a validated vulnerability here.\n\n\n---\n\n### GitHub comments (2)\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-10-28T17:40:51Z)\n>\n> Follow-through on PR #274 at immutable head `5b68e0347366ce83709b45701e4b749b3d28f7a3` (checked 2026-10-28 17:40 UTC): both reported failures have corresponding source corrections, and the Node 26 job now passes.\n> \n> - [Exact-version fixture](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/blob/5b68e0347366ce83709b45701e4b749b3d28f7a3/test/item-history-versions.test.ts) reads the actual local package version, installs every differing requested version into an isolated prefix, and still asserts the resulting version. The matrix now includes full/diff/limit output and recorded-message assertions; project pins are unchanged.\n> - [History service](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/blob/5b68e0347366ce83709b45701e4b749b3d28f7a3/src/services/item-history.ts) explicitly requests full history plus same-snapshot diffs, uses their physical indices, and retains recorded messages (bounded to512characters) in patch-free browser rows. The real-route fixture now asserts `exercise update flags` rather than deleting the contract check.\n> - [Node26 job122972159874](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/actions/runs/40732476840/job/122972159874) completed successfully: npm852/852 tests and Bun852/852 tests, both0failures, with coverage thresholds met and subsequent release checks completed. The named .20/.27/.28 compatibility test passes in both runs. These are inspected hosted logs, not local execution of the whole suite.\n> \n> Independent bounded verification also passes17 checks against the exact compiled helper body with mocked host boundaries: both display orders, same-snapshot indices, recorded message preservation/bounds, patch omission,125-row backward traversal across an append without duplicates, explicit full/diff invocation and mismatched-projection refusal. Exact-version selection/assertion was independently inspected statically; no claim of independently installing all three artifacts here.\n> \n> At this observation Node22 is still running, so its full gates remain pending. The separately reported CodeQL annotation remains a distinct aggregate failure; it is not proof these two original test failures remain. Keep this issue's final acceptance open until the required exact-head matrix completes. [pm-web-lgg5](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/blob/5b68e0347366ce83709b45701e4b749b3d28f7a3/.agents/pm/issues/pm-web-lgg5.toon) remains the implementation owner; [pm-web-f3xo](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/blob/5b68e0347366ce83709b45701e4b749b3d28f7a3/.agents/pm/issues/pm-web-f3xo.toon) explicitly retains the deeper full/diff suffix replay cost. No deployed behavior, persisted-history loss or whole-release certification is inferred.\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-11-02T09:27:10Z)\n>\n> Fixed on main. Evidence: PR #274 merged 2026-10-28T21:30Z (corrections at head 5b68e03: exact-version fixture installs isolated prefixes; history projection contract restored); main CI green runs 40889189656 (2026-10-29), 41131955064, 41203058017 (Found in the 2026-11-02 triage of issues the blind issue watch missed.)"
